  "findings": [
    "Production App/DraftStartup/StorageStartup and controller imported directly. Window.Worker subclasses original Worker and only records events; production parsing is not replaced.",
    "Tauri file inspection/capture/revision results and synthetic messages/drafts are controlled inputs. All 9 PDF data payloads already independently matched full authored files. No native IO or backend Webview proof.",
    "11 planned scenarios cover explicit Start, full-page/possibly-invisible disclosure, PDF page/ordinal location without fixed ordinal, query barriers, Unicode, image-only explicit pdfNoText, four whole-read failures, mixed formats, 3 late owner changes, cancellation and navigation recheck.",
    "Mixed expected 16 matches independently accounts PDF1 + XLSX5 + DOCX8 + TXT2.",
    "Per-run before/after hashes cover src, dependency/config and imported capture maps; page errors/external requests reject, same-origin blob explicitly permitted.",
    "Settings calls and protected draft strings are compared; unexpected IPC rejects. Forbidden Agent commands are checked.",
    "Failure writes exclusive result and retains failure diagnostics; success is not declared until actual browser run."
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Within existing four-failure scenario, assert 05/09 invalid and 06 textLimit rather than any error. Sent to root; not changed here."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Old 01/02 captured fixtures are not queried in current harness; do not claim new hidden/crop/rotation or unknown-mapping search acceptance from this planned run.",
    "maxActive concerns controlled IPC promises, not actual Rust/OS semaphore lifetime.",
    "No automatic exact PDF.js TextItem ordinal expectation; hand model indices are separate.",
    "The image-only success-empty assumption was corrected before browser execution and retained in scenarios.mjs.raw/pre-run-corrections."
  ],
